    "ar": "استبيان المزارعين (ملخصات القرى)"
   },
   "owner": "RESOLVE project team (ESDU, American University of Beirut)",
   "source": "Direct farmer surveys - see instruments chouf_2026 and beqaa_2026",
   "licence": "All rights reserved - research use; contact the RESOLVE team",
   "consent": "Research use only. Public outputs are disclosure-controlled aggregates; no individual record is published.",
   "method": "Answers standardized to controlled vocabularies, resolved to official cadastral units (OCHA COD-AB), and aggregated. A village is published only if at least k respondents answered; otherwise respondents are pooled at district (caza) level. Sensitive indicators (income, age, gender, cost shares) are published at district level only.",
   "caveats": [
    "Respondents were not randomly sampled; figures describe respondents, not whole villages.",
    "Chouf interviews have no recorded dates; Beqaa interviews were on 2026-01-04.",
    "Locations are cadastral areas, never farm or household locations."
   ]
  },
  "fire_detections": {
   "title": {
    "en": "Satellite fire detections",
    "ar": "رصد الحرائق بالأقمار الصناعية"
   },
   "owner": "Unknown - legacy RESOLVE file (fields match NASA FIRMS active-fire exports)",
   "source": "Probably NASA FIRMS (LANCE). Sensor, product version and query are not recorded.",
   "licence": "NASA FIRMS data are free to use with attribution (to be confirmed once the source is re-acquired)",
   "citation": "NASA FIRMS, https://firms.modaps.eosdis.nasa.gov (assumed; unverified)",
   "method": "Points are the centres of satellite pixels (375 m VIIRS or 1 km MODIS - unknown) flagged as thermal anomalies.",
   "caveats": [
    "Not all detections are wildfires; thermal anomalies include agricultural burning and industrial heat.",
    "Detections in South Lebanon rise 4–8× in Sep–Oct 2024, consistent with conflict-related fires.",
    "Confidence and fire radiative power were removed in the legacy file, so low-confidence detections cannot be filtered.",
    "The point marks a pixel centre, not the exact fire location."
   ]
  },
